Hello, I am TextTalk, the Dialogic text to speech converter.
I have an unlimited vocabulary, and I can pronounce any word correctly.

The user can adjust my base pitch. 50 Hertz is the lowest, and
200 Hertz is the highest. 85 Hertz is normal.

I understand how to expand abbreviations.  English has some tricky abbreviations,
like "ST" for street, Saint, and 1st.  "DR", for doctor and drive.
But I can interpret them correctly. I can say, "on the 1st of the month
Dr. Witzlofsky of Pine St., goes to the St. Anne's Hospital, on Harbor Dr.."

I say numbers differently, depending on context.        
With no commas, and no dollar sign,  I say, 387876675274.85.  
With commas, and a dollar sign, I say $387,876,657,675,274.85. 

I say monetary amounts correctly, such as $2,345,678,123.45. 
I know about units of measure, like ft., mi., kg., and lbs...

I can speak faster, this is 200 words per minute.
This can be used for rapid scanning of information.

If necessary,
I can speak slowly, giving the listener time to write down important information ,.

I know how to spell.. For example, wordsmith. ~WORDSMITH..

TextTalk has an intelligent pre-processor
specifically designed to read E-mail messages.

TextTalk is an implementation of TruVoice, the Centigram Text to speech
converter with Dialogic boards.
 
For further information on TextTalk, you may contact Dialogic Sales at 
